1
00:00:26,141 --> 00:00:27,441
Su Ah's dad and I...

2
00:00:28,511 --> 00:00:29,611
got divorced.

3
00:00:37,651 --> 00:00:39,561
What did you just say?

4
00:00:40,661 --> 00:00:41,691
You did what?

5
00:00:42,561 --> 00:00:43,591
We got divorced.

6
00:00:45,401 --> 00:00:46,661
We split up.

7
00:00:47,661 --> 00:00:49,331
Who are you divorcing?

8
00:00:50,431 --> 00:00:52,541
Who do you think? Your brother.

9
00:00:53,741 --> 00:00:56,371
I'm not your sister-in-law anymore.

10
00:01:08,151 --> 00:01:09,151
Mi Seon.

11
00:01:10,421 --> 00:01:13,091
What is it? Am I not allowed to get a divorce?

12
00:01:13,721 --> 00:01:16,631
No, it's just so sudden.

13
00:01:17,591 --> 00:01:19,531
What on earth happened?

14
00:01:20,861 --> 00:01:22,501
Did my brother cheat on you?

15
00:01:22,971 --> 00:01:26,041
Did some woman show up with his secret baby or something?

16
00:01:26,371 --> 00:01:27,841
That's your father's story.

17
00:01:28,841 --> 00:01:30,511
Even though I have never met him.

18
00:01:33,041 --> 00:01:35,881
Well, my late grandfather and my dad both...

19
00:01:36,551 --> 00:01:39,051
That's usually why people get divorced.

20
00:01:39,721 --> 00:01:42,851
Then why are you suddenly divorcing my brother?

21
00:01:42,921 --> 00:01:45,891
It's sudden to you. But for me...

22
00:01:48,731 --> 00:01:51,061
I've been thinking about it for a while.

23
00:01:53,801 --> 00:01:55,101
My mom does not know, right?

24
00:01:55,801 --> 00:01:57,431
He should be the one to tell her.

25
00:01:57,831 --> 00:01:59,041
What about you?

26
00:01:59,101 --> 00:02:01,941
Are you not going to tell my mom and grandmother?

27
00:02:02,841 --> 00:02:04,871
It's obvious they'll try to stop me.

28
00:02:05,641 --> 00:02:07,511
And since I grew up without my own parents,

29
00:02:07,711 --> 00:02:10,411
words from your mother and grandmother, who embraced me...

30
00:02:13,681 --> 00:02:17,151
Their eyes and their silence would make me waver.

31
00:02:17,221 --> 00:02:18,221
I don't want that.

32
00:02:19,761 --> 00:02:22,991
But isn't that a bit too harsh? We are family.

33
00:02:24,691 --> 00:02:25,761
We were family.

34
00:02:28,161 --> 00:02:29,271
And now we're not?

35
00:02:38,511 --> 00:02:40,781
Where is Su Ah? And my brother?

36
00:02:41,611 --> 00:02:43,211
Probably at some local motel.

37
00:02:43,551 --> 00:02:45,981
Did you kick them out of the house? Even Su Ah?

38
00:02:46,451 --> 00:02:49,491
Our apartment went up for auction, Da Mi.

39
00:02:50,521 --> 00:02:53,590
Mom bought you that house. How did...

40
00:02:53,591 --> 00:02:55,631
It has been four months since the taekwondo studio went under, too.

41
00:02:55,991 --> 00:02:57,131
That makes no sense.

42
00:02:57,591 --> 00:02:59,200
I heard it was doing so well...

43
00:02:59,201 --> 00:03:01,001
that you were thinking of opening a second branch.

44
00:03:01,661 --> 00:03:03,171
How did this happen?

45
00:03:03,231 --> 00:03:05,901
My brother is the most hardworking and kind person in the world.

46
00:03:06,371 --> 00:03:08,241
My only crime was living diligently, too.

47
00:03:09,411 --> 00:03:12,111
Actually, if anything is a crime, that would be it.

48
00:03:12,541 --> 00:03:16,311
Being clueless and thinking, "At least my husband is kind,"

49
00:03:17,881 --> 00:03:18,881
and trusting him...

50
00:03:22,051 --> 00:03:24,451
So my brother and Su Ah are at a motel.

51
00:03:24,791 --> 00:03:25,861
Then what about you?

52
00:03:25,991 --> 00:03:27,621
I slept at a 24-hour spa yesterday.

53
00:03:28,321 --> 00:03:30,531
I'm looking for a room with no deposit and monthly rent.

54
00:03:31,731 --> 00:03:34,331
Let's say the business failed, you lost the house, and you are broke.

55
00:03:34,401 --> 00:03:35,601
That's shocking enough,

56
00:03:36,071 --> 00:03:37,901
but you are getting a divorce over money?

57
00:03:37,971 --> 00:03:40,001
Without even telling anyone in the family?

58
00:03:40,441 --> 00:03:43,071
That's why I'm telling you right now.

59
00:03:43,971 --> 00:03:47,081
Da Mi, the reason I decided to get a divorce...

60
00:03:47,141 --> 00:03:49,551
isn't because our business failed and we became beggars.

61
00:03:49,611 --> 00:03:50,650
Then why?

62
00:03:50,651 --> 00:03:53,581
You said he didn't cheat, and it wasn't about money.

63
00:03:54,421 --> 00:03:55,621
Then why on earth?

64
00:03:55,691 --> 00:03:57,551
Even though he has absolutely nothing,

65
00:03:57,621 --> 00:03:59,991
to his friends, acquaintances, and even complete strangers,

66
00:04:01,921 --> 00:04:03,991
he can't ignore anyone if he feels even a little sorry for them.

67
00:04:04,061 --> 00:04:07,031
That's because my brother is just too nice.

68
00:04:07,401 --> 00:04:09,831
He has always been soft-hearted, even when we were young.

69
00:04:09,901 --> 00:04:12,771
Yes, if we are talking about your brother's soft heart,

70
00:04:13,571 --> 00:04:15,441
that darn soft heart of his...

71
00:04:15,501 --> 00:04:19,041
is overflowing so much that it could melt the entire Arctic.

72
00:04:19,511 --> 00:04:22,911
He scraped together all our money behind my back to help and co-sign.

73
00:04:25,721 --> 00:04:27,451
Now all I can do is laugh.

74
00:04:28,121 --> 00:04:29,491
He co-signed a loan?

75
00:04:30,121 --> 00:04:31,921
My mom has been telling us since we were kids...

76
00:04:31,991 --> 00:04:33,921
to never co-sign a loan, not even for family.

77
00:04:33,991 --> 00:04:35,561
She drilled it into our heads.

78
00:04:35,631 --> 00:04:37,090
I bit the bullet and bought him...

79
00:04:37,091 --> 00:04:39,461
a 280-dollar down jacket from an outlet,

80
00:04:39,801 --> 00:04:43,371
but the next day, he gave it to an old man collecting cardboard.

81
00:04:43,401 --> 00:04:45,541
He just can't stand seeing other people suffer.

82
00:04:51,211 --> 00:04:54,541
He gives everything away even when he can barely afford to.

83
00:04:55,141 --> 00:04:57,681
That's nothing but vanity. It's an incurable disease.

84
00:04:58,011 --> 00:05:00,351
It's best to avoid people like him in the first place,

85
00:05:00,721 --> 00:05:02,251
and the smart ones leave early.

86
00:05:03,091 --> 00:05:04,151
That's my conclusion.

87
00:05:04,221 --> 00:05:07,461
My brother does have a bit of a tendency to do that.

88
00:05:08,091 --> 00:05:09,931
- Still... - A bit?

89
00:05:10,491 --> 00:05:11,961
Is this because you are his sister?

90
00:05:12,831 --> 00:05:15,631
Even after everything I just said, you still take his side.

91
00:05:17,631 --> 00:05:22,201
That’s just who Kang Gang Nam is, down to his very bones.

92
00:05:23,241 --> 00:05:25,611
I'm not living with him anymore. I'm leaving.

93
00:05:25,981 --> 00:05:27,181
Mi Seon, wait a second.

94
00:05:29,451 --> 00:05:31,651
Come with me to the ATM right over there.

95
00:05:32,551 --> 00:05:33,581
Why?

96
00:05:33,651 --> 00:05:35,951
Where can you even find a place without a deposit these days?

97
00:05:36,621 --> 00:05:39,021
I can withdraw 5,000 dollars right now.

98
00:05:39,491 --> 00:05:40,861
I will give it to you.

99
00:05:40,921 --> 00:05:43,831
I'm grateful you're not asking me to go back home with you, Da Mi.

100
00:05:44,361 --> 00:05:46,631
As if you would actually come with me if I asked.

101
00:05:48,131 --> 00:05:51,431
Did you buy your mom cheesecake for her birthday yesterday?

102
00:05:52,341 --> 00:05:53,341
Yes.

103
00:05:54,001 --> 00:05:56,171
And that was the only thing you got her, right?

104
00:05:58,411 --> 00:06:01,581
If you have money to help me, give your mom an allowance instead.

105
00:06:02,081 --> 00:06:03,181
You're way too cheap.

106
00:06:04,681 --> 00:06:06,521
Tell her not to worry about me...

107
00:06:06,951 --> 00:06:09,521
and that I will call her once I find a place and a job.

108
00:06:10,591 --> 00:06:11,591
I'm leaving now.

109
00:06:12,961 --> 00:06:13,961
Mi Seon...

110
00:06:14,961 --> 00:06:16,061
Mi Seon.

111
00:06:19,861 --> 00:06:21,301
Am I really that cheap?

112
00:06:25,371 --> 00:06:27,071
Anyway, what am I going to do about this?

113
00:06:27,141 --> 00:06:29,241
Mom is going to pass out when she finds out.

114
00:06:43,551 --> 00:06:47,021
By the way, did you buy any clothes you liked?

115
00:06:47,091 --> 00:06:48,921
Did that manager pick them out for you?

116
00:06:49,191 --> 00:06:51,091
I mean Manager Kang, my personal shopper.

117
00:06:51,491 --> 00:06:53,261
What? Oh, yes.

118
00:06:54,861 --> 00:06:57,201
You know tomorrow is our wedding anniversary, right?

119
00:06:57,671 --> 00:06:59,501
You are coming to the dinner too.

120
00:06:59,941 --> 00:07:02,371
Oh, so that was the important event you mentioned?

121
00:07:02,811 --> 00:07:04,211
Of course I will be there to celebrate.

122
00:07:05,571 --> 00:07:08,081
Did that manager say anything else to you?

123
00:07:09,511 --> 00:07:10,551
Like what?

124
00:07:11,151 --> 00:07:12,881
No, she just picked out the clothes.

125
00:07:14,681 --> 00:07:18,521
Well, I spilled juice the other day.

126
00:07:18,591 --> 00:07:20,561
She must have had a hard time cleaning it up,

127
00:07:20,961 --> 00:07:24,031
so I was just wondering if she mentioned it to you.

128
00:07:24,491 --> 00:07:26,231
She might have shown some annoyance.

129
00:07:29,031 --> 00:07:31,071
Actually, I just ended up completely embarrassing myself.

130
00:07:31,601 --> 00:07:32,601
You embarrassed yourself?

131
00:07:33,801 --> 00:07:35,401
How could my son embarrass himself?

132
00:07:36,311 --> 00:07:37,871
It's nothing you need to worry about.

133
00:07:37,941 --> 00:07:40,881
- It was just a minor incident. - Oh my, did you...

134
00:07:42,181 --> 00:07:43,611
spill juice too?

135
00:07:45,851 --> 00:07:47,751
I wish it had been that simple.

136
00:07:49,121 --> 00:07:50,121
Do Yun.

137
00:07:51,491 --> 00:07:53,691
No. Why would I spill juice?

138
00:07:53,991 --> 00:07:55,121
I will go get Grandma.

139
00:07:59,331 --> 00:08:00,401
An incident?

140
00:08:03,671 --> 00:08:06,101
Anyway, it seems she kept her mouth shut about that day.

141
00:08:08,101 --> 00:08:10,971
Then again, if she breathed a word of it,

142
00:08:11,611 --> 00:08:13,341
I'd make sure she lost her job.

143
00:08:18,611 --> 00:08:19,651
Easy...

144
00:08:19,781 --> 00:08:21,481
Be careful. Yes. Slowly.

145
00:08:24,191 --> 00:08:26,321
- Hurry up, Grandma. - I'm coming.

146
00:08:26,991 --> 00:08:28,461
- Mother. - Yes?

147
00:08:28,521 --> 00:08:32,631
Jin Hee bought the sushi you like today,

148
00:08:32,701 --> 00:08:34,561
- so enjoy your meal. - Okay.

149
00:08:34,961 --> 00:08:38,471
I was just thinking it has been a while since I had some.

150
00:08:39,201 --> 00:08:41,271
- Okay, let's go in. - Yes.

151
00:08:43,271 --> 00:08:45,811
(Always Together Realty)

152
00:08:45,881 --> 00:08:49,281
Please sign here and on the page below.

153
00:08:49,581 --> 00:08:50,751
Yes.

154
00:08:51,381 --> 00:08:53,821
It's in a 30-year-old villa,

155
00:08:53,881 --> 00:08:55,020
but it has new wallpaper and flooring,

156
00:08:55,021 --> 00:08:56,120
and it's been cleaned for move-in.

157
00:08:56,121 --> 00:08:58,051
I paid a lot of attention to it.

158
00:08:59,121 --> 00:09:00,291
Mr. Kang,

159
00:09:00,361 --> 00:09:03,731
this amount is very cheap for a lease.

160
00:09:03,791 --> 00:09:05,661
It's not a full lease. It's a deposit-plus-rent lease.

161
00:09:05,731 --> 00:09:07,301
The monthly rent is quite high.

162
00:09:07,361 --> 00:09:08,431
But...

163
00:09:09,171 --> 00:09:10,571
are you sure it will be okay?

164
00:09:11,371 --> 00:09:13,801
- About what? - Being in the same neighbourhood,

165
00:09:13,871 --> 00:09:17,041
you are bound to run into each other.

166
00:09:17,771 --> 00:09:19,981
Well, I will just try to avoid her,

167
00:09:20,041 --> 00:09:22,311
but if we do run into each other, there is nothing I can do.

168
00:09:22,381 --> 00:09:26,451
Even if you are fine with it, what about your, you know, mistress.

169
00:09:27,751 --> 00:09:30,021
- Oh, come on. - Oh, goodness.

170
00:09:31,421 --> 00:09:36,161
You got officially divorced and moved in together.

171
00:09:36,231 --> 00:09:37,531
I mean your second wife.

172
00:09:38,731 --> 00:09:40,631
- Are we all done here? - Yes.

173
00:09:41,061 --> 00:09:42,631
Oh, my legs.

174
00:09:42,831 --> 00:09:44,031
- Goodness. - Oh, my.

175
00:09:45,371 --> 00:09:46,371
(Always Together Realty)

176
00:09:46,372 --> 00:09:48,341
What are you going to do, Ms. Park?

177
00:09:48,401 --> 00:09:51,011
It's been ages since I put the shop across from mine on the market,

178
00:09:51,071 --> 00:09:52,241
and still no news?

179
00:09:52,311 --> 00:09:55,381
Oh, what brings you here at this hour?

180
00:09:55,441 --> 00:09:56,811
I was so frustrated...

181
00:09:56,881 --> 00:09:58,911
that I came right after closing my shop.

182
00:09:59,181 --> 00:10:02,891
Just because I trusted you with it, are you slacking off?

183
00:10:03,751 --> 00:10:07,391
Real estate agencies are everywhere these days.

184
00:10:08,021 --> 00:10:11,031
What should I do? Should I switch to another one?

185
00:10:12,261 --> 00:10:14,401
Oh, come on.

186
00:10:14,461 --> 00:10:16,931
Why would you say something so hurtful?

187
00:10:17,271 --> 00:10:18,271
Who is that?

188
00:10:19,301 --> 00:10:20,671
Pardon?

189
00:10:20,741 --> 00:10:22,971
The man who just hid over there.

190
00:10:23,241 --> 00:10:25,841
Oh, well... Who do you mean?

191
00:10:25,911 --> 00:10:27,381
It's nobody.

192
00:10:27,711 --> 00:10:31,651
Do you have a boyfriend? Just whisper it to me.

193
00:10:32,311 --> 00:10:34,551
My lips are sealed.

194
00:10:36,591 --> 00:10:37,591
Mother.

195
00:10:42,861 --> 00:10:44,491
Whose son is he?

196
00:10:45,031 --> 00:10:47,361
From what I saw, he looked quite handsome.

197
00:10:48,531 --> 00:10:50,631
I told you, my lips are sealed.

198
00:11:02,751 --> 00:11:05,651
I should've found a way to give her the 5,000 dollars.

199
00:11:07,381 --> 00:11:09,751
Why are there so many incidents and accidents today?

200
00:11:19,031 --> 00:11:21,801
- Oh, my gosh! - Wait, why is this here...

201
00:11:26,271 --> 00:11:27,271
Please give it to me.

202
00:11:29,541 --> 00:11:30,771
What a pervert.

203
00:11:31,271 --> 00:11:32,410
If he has any shame,

204
00:11:32,411 --> 00:11:34,341
he won't come looking for me again, right?

205
00:11:36,081 --> 00:11:37,650
Good thing I failed...

206
00:11:37,651 --> 00:11:38,981
the internship application for Hwanggeum Apparel.

207
00:11:39,051 --> 00:11:41,721
If I had passed, I would have met him as my boss.

208
00:11:48,291 --> 00:11:49,931
Anyway, Kang Gang Nam.

209
00:11:50,331 --> 00:11:53,301
How am I supposed to bring up Mi Seon's situation to Mom?

210
00:11:53,901 --> 00:11:56,000
You little punk!

211
00:11:56,001 --> 00:11:58,101
You're just bringing this up now?

212
00:11:58,171 --> 00:12:01,101
After making such a mess, who do you expect to clean it up?

213
00:12:01,171 --> 00:12:03,371
How dare you show up with that, you punk?

214
00:12:03,441 --> 00:12:05,741
Mom! That hurts!

215
00:12:05,811 --> 00:12:06,881
Gosh, stop it.

216
00:12:07,911 --> 00:12:09,551
That hurts! I'm sorry.

217
00:12:09,611 --> 00:12:11,781
- You punk. - Hey, Kang Da Mi.

218
00:12:11,851 --> 00:12:13,121
- Stop, Mom, please. - Why you...

219
00:12:13,181 --> 00:12:15,121
Your brother is going to get beaten to death!

220
00:12:15,181 --> 00:12:17,521
Why are you just standing there? Hurry up and grab him!

221
00:12:17,921 --> 00:12:19,521
Hey! Why are you grabbing me?

222
00:12:19,591 --> 00:12:21,560
Why you little rascal!

223
00:12:21,561 --> 00:12:23,461
Stop!

224
00:12:25,091 --> 00:12:29,061
Mom. I'm going to be 40 soon.

225
00:12:29,601 --> 00:12:31,771
Please stop hitting me. It really hurts.

226
00:12:32,101 --> 00:12:33,241
Forty?

227
00:12:33,301 --> 00:12:35,371
I'm turning 60 any day now, you punk.

228
00:12:35,441 --> 00:12:37,671
How dare you try to use your age against me?

229
00:12:37,741 --> 00:12:40,311
You blew your money, got divorced, and dare to say that?

230
00:12:40,381 --> 00:12:42,641
- Mom. - You punk!

231
00:12:42,711 --> 00:12:45,651
That hardworking and sweet Mi Seon...

232
00:12:45,711 --> 00:12:47,521
Imagine how broken her heart must have been...

233
00:12:47,781 --> 00:12:50,251
Imagine how miserable she must have felt...

234
00:12:50,321 --> 00:12:51,451
to sign those divorce papers...

235
00:12:51,521 --> 00:12:53,691
and walk out of the house on her own.

236
00:12:53,761 --> 00:12:55,691
- You punk! - Goodness.

237
00:12:56,461 --> 00:12:59,761
Use your words, Mom. Su Ah is probably here, too.

238
00:13:01,361 --> 00:13:04,471
I knew it was too quiet these past few years.

239
00:13:04,871 --> 00:13:06,370
I was so proud to buy you two a house,

240
00:13:06,371 --> 00:13:08,601
and I finally slept peacefully with my arms and legs stretched out.

241
00:13:09,001 --> 00:13:11,241
Did I think a day like this would ever come?

242
00:13:12,371 --> 00:13:15,611
Wait, did you cheat on her by any chance?

243
00:13:16,651 --> 00:13:17,781
Mom.

244
00:13:18,411 --> 00:13:20,621
Who are you comparing me to?

245
00:13:21,321 --> 00:13:22,751
Am I Kang Hak Sung?

246
00:13:23,051 --> 00:13:25,891
Right, Mom. He says that's not it.

247
00:13:26,891 --> 00:13:28,291
How do you know that?

248
00:13:28,921 --> 00:13:29,991
Did you meet Mi Seon?

249
00:13:31,191 --> 00:13:32,191
What?

250
00:13:32,261 --> 00:13:35,661
Oh, I'm actually on my way back from meeting her.

251
00:13:36,001 --> 00:13:38,431
See, I told you, didn't I?

252
00:13:38,501 --> 00:13:42,341
And I wanted to split up anyway.

253
00:13:43,441 --> 00:13:44,571
Why would you?

254
00:13:44,641 --> 00:13:46,711
- With what nerve? - Well...

255
00:13:48,511 --> 00:13:50,511
Ever since Su Ah was potty trained,

256
00:13:51,111 --> 00:13:52,651
she wouldn't let me even go near her.

257
00:13:52,981 --> 00:13:56,221
- What does that mean, Mom? - Are you kidding me right now?

258
00:13:56,791 --> 00:13:58,021
Why won't she let you near her?

259
00:13:59,251 --> 00:14:00,491
Have you two been sleeping in separate rooms?

260
00:14:02,721 --> 00:14:05,731
Oh, they say there are a lot of couples like that these days.

261
00:14:05,791 --> 00:14:07,431
I saw it in an article.

262
00:14:07,831 --> 00:14:09,831
Stay out of this. What do you know?

263
00:14:10,901 --> 00:14:12,201
Why would you sleep in separate rooms?

264
00:14:13,771 --> 00:14:15,401
Is there something wrong with you?

265
00:14:15,471 --> 00:14:17,441
What? Come on...

266
00:14:17,871 --> 00:14:19,111
Listen,

267
00:14:19,171 --> 00:14:22,811
I'm always ready to go, day or night.

268
00:14:25,181 --> 00:14:26,521
Do you know...

269
00:14:26,821 --> 00:14:30,591
how miserable I have been for the past few years?

270
00:14:31,121 --> 00:14:33,021
I can't even tell you how much my self-esteem...

271
00:14:33,091 --> 00:14:36,331
as a man has plummeted.

272
00:14:36,591 --> 00:14:37,961
So, Mom.

273
00:14:38,361 --> 00:14:41,931
Please stop hitting your oldest son. It hurts. It really hurts.

274
00:14:42,931 --> 00:14:45,771
Everyone has their own secrets they can't talk about.

275
00:14:52,811 --> 00:14:56,251
So, what you're saying is...

276
00:14:56,311 --> 00:14:58,811
your dad slept in the tiny room,

277
00:14:59,411 --> 00:15:02,581
and you and your mom slept in the master bedroom?

278
00:15:02,951 --> 00:15:05,991
No, I sleep in my own room.

279
00:15:06,761 --> 00:15:09,161
My goodness, what is this?

280
00:15:09,631 --> 00:15:13,731
So your mom slept in the master bedroom all by herself,

281
00:15:13,801 --> 00:15:15,831
and your dad slept in the tiny room...

282
00:15:15,901 --> 00:15:18,231
with the refrigerator and the kimchi refrigerator?

283
00:15:19,031 --> 00:15:21,841
- Since when? - Since a long, long time ago.

284
00:15:23,611 --> 00:15:25,871
This is driving me crazy.

285
00:15:29,851 --> 00:15:31,881
Why are you pushing me?

286
00:15:31,951 --> 00:15:34,121
- Oh, come on. - Aunt Da Mi.

287
00:15:34,181 --> 00:15:37,891
Oh, is our Su Ah here? Oh, you are so pretty.

288
00:15:38,391 --> 00:15:39,421
Follow me.

289
00:15:39,861 --> 00:15:41,791
Hey, Mi Mi.

290
00:15:41,861 --> 00:15:42,931
What?

291
00:15:43,391 --> 00:15:45,561
Look, your oldest son...

292
00:15:45,961 --> 00:15:47,701
has been living like a neglected husband.

293
00:15:48,031 --> 00:15:49,301
Are you enjoying this?

294
00:15:49,901 --> 00:15:51,771
I'm just so dumbfounded.

295
00:15:51,831 --> 00:15:53,341
According to Su Ah, he has been sleeping alone...

296
00:15:53,401 --> 00:15:54,671
in that tiny room.

297
00:15:54,771 --> 00:15:58,611
Listening to the refrigerators humming all night,

298
00:15:58,671 --> 00:16:00,341
your oldest son has been sleeping all by himself.

299
00:16:00,411 --> 00:16:01,441
Does that make any sense?

300
00:16:02,581 --> 00:16:04,311
Is Gang Nam here?

301
00:16:05,181 --> 00:16:06,551
- Yes. - Oh my.

302
00:16:06,981 --> 00:16:11,291
- My little sweetie is here too. - Great-Grandma, I missed you.

303
00:16:12,091 --> 00:16:15,321
Yes, I feel the same way.

304
00:16:15,591 --> 00:16:18,761
But why didn't you come over on your grandma's birthday?

305
00:16:18,831 --> 00:16:21,730
Mom and Dad were fighting.

306
00:16:21,731 --> 00:16:23,601
They were fighting so much that...

307
00:16:23,901 --> 00:16:24,901
Su Ah.

308
00:16:26,501 --> 00:16:29,371
Dad told you it was a secret.

309
00:16:30,741 --> 00:16:32,071
Some secret.

310
00:16:32,541 --> 00:16:35,781
Gang Nam, kids hear everything.

311
00:16:36,111 --> 00:16:37,211
Traitor.

312
00:16:37,551 --> 00:16:39,181
What's going on?

313
00:16:39,251 --> 00:16:40,751
Well, Mrs. Choi.

314
00:16:40,851 --> 00:16:43,151
It seems the oldest couple...

315
00:16:43,221 --> 00:16:45,091
Mother, please go into your room.

316
00:16:45,621 --> 00:16:47,021
I will tell you everything.

317
00:16:47,091 --> 00:16:48,191
All right.

318
00:16:48,891 --> 00:16:50,031
Let's hear it.

319
00:16:59,431 --> 00:17:00,871
You are a traitor.

320
00:17:01,371 --> 00:17:03,141
Su Ah, let's go to my room.

321
00:17:05,541 --> 00:17:08,581
So they decided to split up?

322
00:17:08,941 --> 00:17:10,381
Sit comfortably.

323
00:17:10,781 --> 00:17:13,781
You are turning 60 soon.

324
00:17:14,051 --> 00:17:17,051
Do your joints still feel like they're 20 years old?

325
00:17:17,721 --> 00:17:19,791
You must be very confident.

326
00:17:21,061 --> 00:17:22,821
It's my fault...

327
00:17:24,061 --> 00:17:25,691
for raising him poorly, Mother.

328
00:17:25,761 --> 00:17:28,201
You can give birth to a child, but you can't control their mind.

329
00:17:29,401 --> 00:17:30,771
I'm sorry, Grandma.

330
00:17:30,831 --> 00:17:34,471
You're apologising to the wrong person.

331
00:17:36,171 --> 00:17:41,011
You need to beg your mother for her forgiveness.

332
00:17:45,111 --> 00:17:46,111
Gang Nam.

333
00:17:46,781 --> 00:17:49,891
So Mi Seon left and is staying at a 24-hour spa?

334
00:17:50,521 --> 00:17:51,651
Is that true?

335
00:17:53,421 --> 00:17:54,491
Yes.

336
00:17:55,361 --> 00:17:57,831
What a thoughtless person.

337
00:17:59,031 --> 00:18:00,760
Mi Mi, go to the 24-hour spa tomorrow...

338
00:18:00,761 --> 00:18:03,271
and bring Mi Seon to me right away.

339
00:18:03,731 --> 00:18:04,731
Me?

340
00:18:06,371 --> 00:18:09,401
How do I bring back someone who signed the divorce papers?

341
00:18:10,071 --> 00:18:12,541
Even if they are going their separate ways,

342
00:18:12,611 --> 00:18:15,611
make sure she has a place to live before kicking her out.

343
00:18:15,981 --> 00:18:19,151
How could you do that to a girl who has no family to fall back on?

344
00:18:20,351 --> 00:18:21,721
Yes, Mother.

345
00:18:51,511 --> 00:18:55,181
Every child turns out differently.

346
00:18:55,851 --> 00:18:57,351
But at least you have...

347
00:18:57,421 --> 00:19:00,161
the most wonderful son in the world, Dae Chi.

348
00:19:00,591 --> 00:19:02,361
And it is not just Dae Chi, right?

349
00:19:02,421 --> 00:19:04,491
And you also have Da Mi, the daughter you've raised...

350
00:19:04,561 --> 00:19:07,461
all these years, even though you didn't give birth to her.

351
00:19:08,831 --> 00:19:10,331
Who knows?

352
00:19:10,631 --> 00:19:13,801
Maybe that stingy girl will eventually be generous enough...

353
00:19:13,871 --> 00:19:15,871
to send you on a cruise vacation.

354
00:19:17,811 --> 00:19:19,511
I just want her to get married.

355
00:19:19,881 --> 00:19:23,111
Da Mi is incredibly ambitious on the inside.

356
00:19:23,211 --> 00:19:24,411
She has it all figured out...

357
00:19:24,481 --> 00:19:25,981
and will marry into a wealthy family,

358
00:19:26,051 --> 00:19:28,081
so don't even worry about that.

359
00:19:28,281 --> 00:19:29,551
Just let it go.

360
00:19:30,721 --> 00:19:33,591
You will be lucky if she doesn't pretend she does not know you.

361
00:19:35,061 --> 00:19:36,261
What are you talking about?

362
00:19:36,321 --> 00:19:38,991
Why would my daughter, Da Mi, pretend not to know me?

363
00:19:39,261 --> 00:19:41,361
Well, you know...

364
00:19:41,561 --> 00:19:44,270
There is an old saying that you should never take in a stray human.

365
00:19:44,271 --> 00:19:45,671
People say that for a reason.

366
00:19:55,011 --> 00:19:57,311
What are you looking for?

367
00:19:58,051 --> 00:19:59,611
I'm looking for my sewing kit. Why?

368
00:20:00,351 --> 00:20:01,751
Why do you need your sewing kit?

369
00:20:03,551 --> 00:20:06,821
I'm going to sew that big mouth of yours shut today.

370
00:20:06,891 --> 00:20:08,321
I simply can't take it anymore.

371
00:20:12,561 --> 00:20:13,631
Oh, my.

372
00:20:15,261 --> 00:20:17,371
You are such a brave girl, Su Ah.

373
00:20:17,431 --> 00:20:19,301
You aren't even crying for your mom.

374
00:20:19,801 --> 00:20:22,341
I promised my mom I wouldn't cry anymore, Aunt Da Mi.

375
00:20:23,371 --> 00:20:24,641
Is that so?

376
00:20:24,711 --> 00:20:26,511
Yes. Mom said that once she makes some money...

377
00:20:26,581 --> 00:20:28,081
and finds a place for us to live,

378
00:20:28,141 --> 00:20:29,711
she will definitely come back to get me.

379
00:20:31,311 --> 00:20:34,381
Your mom said that.

380
00:20:34,451 --> 00:20:37,521
Yes. Aunt Da Mi, what about my dress?

381
00:20:38,821 --> 00:20:39,961
Oh, right.

382
00:20:45,731 --> 00:20:46,901
Ta-da.

383
00:20:47,231 --> 00:20:48,561
What do you think? Do you like it?

384
00:20:51,371 --> 00:20:52,901
Can you add a ribbon to it?

385
00:20:53,641 --> 00:20:56,171
A really big one, please?

386
00:20:56,571 --> 00:20:57,811
You got it.

387
00:20:58,271 --> 00:21:00,741
Just wait a little bit, my sweet niece.

388
00:21:01,011 --> 00:21:05,311
I will attach a giant ribbon and make you an amazing dress...

389
00:21:05,381 --> 00:21:07,881
that even Audrey Hepburn would envy.

390
00:21:09,551 --> 00:21:10,591
Come here.

391
00:21:11,051 --> 00:21:12,151
Oh, my.

392
00:21:18,261 --> 00:21:22,231
(Yeongyeong Bathhouse, 24-Hour Spa)

393
00:21:23,401 --> 00:21:25,171
If she left here too,

394
00:21:25,231 --> 00:21:28,640
- where on earth did she go? - I tried to stop her,

395
00:21:28,641 --> 00:21:29,841
but she said she found a place to live...

396
00:21:29,911 --> 00:21:31,511
and left early this morning.

397
00:21:31,571 --> 00:21:33,141
It didn't seem like she had much money either.

398
00:21:33,211 --> 00:21:36,081
She gave me two credit cards, but neither of them went through.

399
00:21:36,681 --> 00:21:38,211
She ended up paying in cash.

400
00:21:39,781 --> 00:21:42,850
If she happens to come back, please call me right away.

401
00:21:42,851 --> 00:21:44,151
Of course, I will.

402
00:21:44,221 --> 00:21:45,591
By the way,

403
00:21:45,651 --> 00:21:48,991
do you know there is a strange rumour going around your neighbourhood?

404
00:21:49,421 --> 00:21:50,431
What rumour?

405
00:21:51,961 --> 00:21:53,131
I'm busy.

406
00:21:53,191 --> 00:21:54,731
It's probably nonsense, so never mind.

407
00:21:54,801 --> 00:21:56,601
I'm leaving. Hope you get a lot of customers.

408
00:21:56,671 --> 00:21:59,431
Okay. Do not worry too much.

409
00:21:59,801 --> 00:22:02,171
If she really needs to, she'll contact you first.

410
00:22:08,381 --> 00:22:10,851
Goodness, it smells like a bachelor pad.

411
00:22:11,411 --> 00:22:14,281
I told Dae Chi to at least air the place out regularly.

412
00:22:16,151 --> 00:22:18,251
Well, I will let it slide since he is my son.

413
00:22:19,321 --> 00:22:20,391
Okay...

414
00:22:21,591 --> 00:22:24,231
Oh my, what is this?

415
00:22:24,291 --> 00:22:25,631
Why is he drinking so much?

416
00:22:26,091 --> 00:22:27,561
What if he ruins his health?

417
00:22:30,831 --> 00:22:32,571
Is work stressing him out?

418
00:22:43,651 --> 00:22:46,181
What is this? It's a seizure notice.

419
00:22:47,451 --> 00:22:50,021
Why is this on my successful son's house?

420
00:22:54,291 --> 00:22:57,691
(List of Seized Items)

421
00:22:57,761 --> 00:22:59,231
Oh my.

422
00:23:00,501 --> 00:23:05,701
What on earth did this crazy kid do?

423
00:23:08,271 --> 00:23:10,111
Oh my goodness.

424
00:23:10,171 --> 00:23:12,771
This kid, seriously.

425
00:23:13,781 --> 00:23:14,781
Oh my.

426
00:23:32,361 --> 00:23:35,231
So this is what a five-star hotel looks like.

427
00:23:36,001 --> 00:23:38,231
I get to visit a place like this thanks to Dae Chi.

428
00:23:39,301 --> 00:23:41,001
In a hotel restaurant like this,

429
00:23:41,071 --> 00:23:43,171
even a leather shoe would taste good.

430
00:23:52,781 --> 00:23:53,781
That's a relief.

431
00:24:04,391 --> 00:24:05,431
Welcome.

432
00:24:05,961 --> 00:24:07,061
Do you have a reservation?

433
00:24:07,801 --> 00:24:08,861
Under Kang Dae Chi.

434
00:24:12,271 --> 00:24:13,301
Right this way.

435
00:24:26,981 --> 00:24:28,521
(Mom)

436
00:24:33,961 --> 00:24:34,990
You made it.

437
00:24:34,991 --> 00:24:37,490
People making a six-figure salary sure hang out in different places.

438
00:24:37,491 --> 00:24:38,531
Why did you call me?

439
00:24:39,161 --> 00:24:41,631
This is your first time at a place like this, right?

440
00:24:42,161 --> 00:24:43,971
Stop acting like a tourist and sit down.

441
00:24:50,171 --> 00:24:51,971
What do you have to say that we had to meet here?

442
00:24:52,571 --> 00:24:56,081
And if you wanted to spend money, you should have brought Mom here.

443
00:24:56,951 --> 00:24:58,311
Did you do anything for Mom's birthday?

444
00:24:58,851 --> 00:25:01,051
Did you at least send her some money?

445
00:25:01,081 --> 00:25:03,151
I will take care of Mom myself.

446
00:25:06,151 --> 00:25:07,161
Today,

447
00:25:08,291 --> 00:25:10,020
I specifically asked to see you...

448
00:25:10,021 --> 00:25:11,191
because I have something to tell you.

449
00:25:11,261 --> 00:25:14,001
What is it? I'm busy. Just get to the point.

450
00:25:15,101 --> 00:25:16,901
This is a top-tier restaurant.

451
00:25:17,231 --> 00:25:18,431
Da Mi, when you hear what I have to say,

452
00:25:18,501 --> 00:25:19,931
you can't lose your temper.

453
00:25:21,401 --> 00:25:22,871
I got it.

454
00:25:22,941 --> 00:25:26,441
I want to hear what you have to say, eat my steak, and go home.

455
00:25:26,741 --> 00:25:29,411
I will listen to you elegantly and politely,

456
00:25:30,451 --> 00:25:31,511
so get to the point.

457
00:25:34,681 --> 00:25:37,391
Did you get into trouble with some weird woman?

458
00:25:37,821 --> 00:25:38,891
It's nothing like that.

459
00:25:44,961 --> 00:25:45,961
Kang Da Mi.

460
00:25:47,061 --> 00:25:48,531
My one and only sister.

461
00:25:51,471 --> 00:25:52,731
Please lend me 200,000 dollars.

462
00:25:55,741 --> 00:25:57,171
Did you just say 200,000 dollars?

463
00:25:58,141 --> 00:25:59,671
Not 2,000 dollars, not 20,000 dollars,

464
00:26:00,041 --> 00:26:01,111
but 200,000 dollars?

465
00:26:03,011 --> 00:26:04,181
Hey! Are you nuts?

466
00:26:06,651 --> 00:26:07,851
Darn it.

467
00:26:08,251 --> 00:26:09,251
Hey.

468
00:26:18,161 --> 00:26:19,331
Hold on a second.

469
00:26:22,161 --> 00:26:23,331
Thank you.

470
00:26:29,201 --> 00:26:30,311
Crazy jerk.

471
00:26:30,571 --> 00:26:33,171
How did he know I saved up exactly 200,000 dollars?

472
00:26:33,241 --> 00:26:34,811
He makes over 100,000 dollars a year,

473
00:26:34,881 --> 00:26:36,511
and he wants what from a lowly employee like me?

474
00:26:36,581 --> 00:26:37,811
He wants to borrow 200,000 dollars?

475
00:26:39,381 --> 00:26:40,781
This is unbelievable.

476
00:26:51,761 --> 00:26:55,501
Do you have something to say to me?

477
00:26:56,231 --> 00:26:59,771
I'm asking because you keep staring at me.

478
00:26:59,831 --> 00:27:00,841
I'm sorry.

479
00:27:00,901 --> 00:27:03,871
I was just looking because you have a great sense of style.

480
00:27:05,771 --> 00:27:06,771
Right.

481
00:27:07,881 --> 00:27:09,641
They are all so cliche.

482
00:27:09,711 --> 00:27:12,481
This is why social media turns perfectly fine men into idiots.

483
00:27:16,651 --> 00:27:17,991
(Sibling 2)

484
00:27:34,171 --> 00:27:35,501
Hey...

485
00:27:36,271 --> 00:27:37,641
Are you okay?

486
00:27:42,911 --> 00:27:43,911
Goodness.

487
00:27:47,481 --> 00:27:49,481
Hey, are you okay? What should I do?

488
00:28:10,001 --> 00:28:12,141
(Mission: Mompossible)

489
00:28:13,141 --> 00:28:14,811
But how did Assistant Manager Kang...

490
00:28:14,881 --> 00:28:16,981
What era are we living in for parents to step in...

491
00:28:17,051 --> 00:28:19,011
and choose their children's partners?

492
00:28:19,081 --> 00:28:21,981
And you, shouldn't Seung Yun come first?

493
00:28:22,451 --> 00:28:23,791
You must not lose consciousness.

494
00:28:24,321 --> 00:28:25,951
Oh, why be embarrassed in a situation like this?

495
00:28:26,021 --> 00:28:28,061
It's not like we're going to see each other again anyway.

496
00:28:34,061 --> 00:28:36,501
(Mission: Mompossible)
